# Suppression rules for the demo, to show what a real one looks like.
#
#   leakhunter --suppressions poc/docindex.supp build/poc/docindex
#
# The scenario: the indexer leak (bug #4) is in a component owned by another
# team and is already tracked in a ticket. You want CI to stop failing on it
# while still failing on everything else.
#
# The report will still say, in summary.suppressedByRules and in a notice at the
# top of the HTML, exactly what was hidden and by which rule. A suppression makes
# a finding stop counting; it never makes it disappear.

# Bug #4 -- tracked, not forgotten.
file:*/poc/src/IndexWorker.cpp

# Leaving the other three unsuppressed on purpose: the run still exits 1, which
# is what you want from a gate. Add these to silence the rest, one at a time:
#
#   file:*/poc/src/RecordParser.cpp
#   function:*buildDocument*
#   function:*copyPayload*
